"You can use the standard `jakarta.transaction.Transactional` annotation with "
"Hibernate Reactive.\n"
"This provides a more familiar programming model for developers coming from "
"Hibernate ORM."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"While defining transaction handling using the annotation, you should inject "
"`Mutiny.Session` or `Mutiny.StatelessSession` using CDI and use them in "
"methods annotated with `@Transactional`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Here's an example showing how to use `@Transactional` in a REST resource:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Inject the reactive session directly"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use `@Transactional` for persist operations - creates new entities in the "
"database"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use `@Transactional` for update operations - modifies existing entities"
msgstr ""

msgid "The `@Transactional` interceptor will:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Lazily open a Hibernate Reactive session when first accessed"
msgstr ""

msgid "Begin a transaction automatically"
msgstr ""

msgid "Commit the transaction when the `Uni` completes successfully"
