msgid "Activate/deactivate persistence units"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When a persistence unit is configured at build time, and it is assigned "
"entity types or an xref:datasource.adoc#datasource-active[active "
"datasource], the persistence unit is active by default.\n"
"Quarkus starts the corresponding Hibernate Reactive `SessionFactory` when "
"the application starts."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To deactivate a persistence unit at runtime, see xref:hibernate-orm."
"adoc#persistence-unit-active[the corresponding section of the Hibernate ORM "
"guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you decide to follow the example from the Hibernate ORM guide to declare "
"a custom CDI bean for the active persistence unit,\n"
"but you use Hibernate Reactive,\n"
"make sure to work with the `Mutiny.SessionFactory` type instead of `Session`:"
"\n"
"this is one way Hibernate Reactive's API entrypoint differs from Hibernate "
"ORM's."
msgstr ""

msgid "See <<hr-cdi-integration>> for details."
msgstr ""

msgid "Automatically transitioning to Flyway to Manage Schemas"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hibernate Reactive can be used in the same application as Flyway.\n"
"See xref:flyway.adoc#reactive-datasources[this section of the Flyway "
"extension documentation]\n"
"for details regarding configuration of Flyway in a reactive application."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you have the xref:flyway.adoc[Flyway extension] installed when running in "
"development mode,\n"
"Quarkus provides a simple way to initialize your Flyway configuration\n"
"using the schema generated automatically by Hibernate Reactive."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"See xref:hibernate-orm.adoc#flyway[the Hibernate ORM guide] for more details."
""
msgstr ""

