msgid "Limitations and other things you should know"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus does not modify the libraries it uses; this rule applies to "
"Hibernate Reactive as well: when using\n"
"this extension you will mostly have the same experience as using the "
"original library."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"But while they share the same code, Quarkus does configure some components "
"automatically and inject custom implementations\n"
"for some extension points; this should be transparent and useful but if "
"you're an expert of Hibernate Reactive you might want to\n"
"know what is being done."
msgstr ""

msgid "General limitations"
msgstr ""

msgid "Hibernate Reactive is not configurable via a `persistence.xml` file."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This extension only considers the default persistence unit at the moment:\n"
"it's not possible to configure multiple persistence units,\n"
"or even a single named persistence unit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This extension does not support xref:hibernate-orm.adoc#database-"
"approach[database-based multitenancy]\n"
"or xref:hibernate-orm.adoc#schema-approach[schema-based multitenancy] at the "
"moment.\n"
"xref:hibernate-orm.adoc#discriminator-approach[Discriminator-based "
"multitenancy], on the other hand, is expected to work correctly.\n"
"See https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/15959."
msgstr ""

msgid "Integration with the Envers extension is not supported."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Transaction management: choosing between <code>@Transactional</code> and "
"Panache annotations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With the introduction of the `quarkus-reactive-transactions` extension, you "
"now have two options for managing transactions in Hibernate Reactive "
"applications:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use `jakarta.transaction.Transactional` for declarative transaction "
"management"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use Panache's transaction annotations (`@WithTransaction`, `@WithSession`, "
"`@WithSessionOnDemand`, or the programmatic `Panache.withTransaction()`)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You must choose one approach and use it consistently throughout your "
"application.\n"
"Mixing both transaction management styles in the same reactive pipeline is "
"not supported and will result in an `UnsupportedOperationException`.\n"
"In the future, we'll deprecate the previous annotations provided by Panache "
"and and support only `@Transactional`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can inject either `Mutiny.Session` or `Mutiny.StatelessSession`.\n"
"Mixing both session types in the same transaction should work, but should be "
"reserved for exotic use cases implemented by advanced users, as the "
"(stateful) session will not be aware of changes operated through the "
"stateless session, which could thus conflict or be silently erased by "
"(stateful) session writes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Using Declarative Transaction Management in different reactive pipelines"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When using declarative transaction management with Vert.x context-based "
"interceptors (`@Transactional`, `@WithTransaction`, `@WithSession`, "
"`@WithSessionOnDemand`) in multiple methods and combining such methods with "
"either `Uni.combine().all().unis()` or `Uni.join().all()` the same "
"transaction might be shared by different reactive pipelines causing "
"unpredictable behavior."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For this reason, **avoid using declarative transactional management with "
"those methods**."
msgstr ""

msgid "Other Declarative Transactional Management limitations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Reactive transactions does not use `TransactionManager`, thus they are local "
"only and do not support XA transactions. Every parameter defined on the "
"`TransactionManager` (such as `quarkus.transaction-manager.default-"
"transaction-timeout`) will be ignored. Only a single datasource can "
"participate in a transaction."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Reactive transactions also work exclusively within the reactive pipeline.\n"
"If blocking code is executed (for example on a worker thread) as part of "
"that pipeline, it will not be able to participate in the transaction."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Declarative reactive transactions with `@Transactional` can only be applied "
"to methods returning `Uni`, not `Multi`, `CompletionStage`, or "
"`CompletableFuture`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Currently, only `Transactional.TxType.REQUIRED` is supported with reactive "
"transactions. Other transaction types (`REQUIRES_NEW`, `MANDATORY`, etc.) "
"will throw an `UnsupportedOperationException`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Simplifying Hibernate Reactive with Panache"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The xref:hibernate-reactive-panache.adoc[Hibernate Reactive with Panache] "
"extension facilitates the usage of Hibernate Reactive\n"
"by providing active record style entities (and repositories) and focuses on "
"making your entities trivial and fun to write in Quarkus."
msgstr ""

msgid "Validation modes and Hibernate Validator integration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To find out more on how the <<quarkus-hibernate-orm_quarkus-hibernate-orm-"
"validation-mode,`quarkus.hibernate-orm.validation.mode` configuration "
"property>>.\n"
"influence your Hibernate Reactive application see the xref:hibernate-orm."
"adoc#validator_integration[corresponding Hibernate ORM guide],\n"
"as these modes work the same in both cases."
msgstr ""

msgid "Configuration Reference for Hibernate Reactive"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You will notice that some properties\n"
"contain \"jdbc\" in their name: this is because Hibernate ORM refers to its "
"\"data access\" layer as \"JDBC\" for historical reasons. Hibernate Reactive "
"uses Vert.x Reactive SQL clients for its data access layer rather than JDBC."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Regardless of their name, these properties still make sense for Hibernate "
"Reactive."
msgstr ""
